gítimas, como necesidades específicas o precios de mercado.\nQué se puede revisar: Comprobar si los contratos [1], [2], [3] atienden la misma necesidad. Verificar si el adjudicatario A repite contratos en otros sectores. Analizar si los contratos de diciembre se relacionan con otros adjudicatarios en el mismo periodo.","en":"What the data shows: Between 2023 and 2025, this body awarded 141 minor contracts for works above 37,500 and up to 40,000 euros, just under the legal limit. If those amounts were spread as in the band immediately below, 33.8 contracts would be expected. The observed-to-expected ratio is 4.2, with a 95% confidence interval of 3.3 to 5.2. December accounts for 4% of the contracts just under the limit, compared with 7% of all its works contracts. The contracts just under the limit are spread across 86 different awardees. Contract [1], for 37,893 euros, was awarded in May 2025.\nWhat it cannot show: The fact that many contracts are just under the legal limit does not prove any wrongdoing. It could be due to market prices, budget constraints, or separate needs. Statistical indicators like this do not indicate improper actions by individuals or organizations.\nWhat can be checked: Check the details of contract [1] to see what was purchased and the dates. Verify if multiple contracts cover the same need. Look at the distribution of contracts across different awardees to identify patterns or anomalies.","origen_es":"modelo","origen_en":"modelo","modelo":"Qwen3-4B (Q4_K_M, llama.cpp)","regla":"obras","citas":["PieFguk7LGcwYTJJ03sHog%3D%3D","IwjL5jRWZfU7%2B9FIQYNjeQ%3D%3D","wOEi4UwlrovkY6rls5tG9A%3D%3D"],"generado":"2026-11-15"}}